WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.802
-Hey, guys, I'm about to
show you some books

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.037
that you should avoid
at all costs.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.538
It is time for the latest
installment of my

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.139
"Do Not Read" list.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.974 line:0%
♪ Do not read ♪

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.343 line:0%
♪ Do not read ♪

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.944 line:0%
♪ Do not read these books ♪

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:13.846 line:0%
♪ These books ♪

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.715
-Now, before we start,
I just want you to know that

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:18.651
every book that I'm about to
show you is 100% real.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.086
These are actual books.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.887
You can find them on Amazon
or check them out

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.055
at your local library.

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:24.624
They are real.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.593
Alright, let's see what's on
my "Do Not Read" list.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:31.497
This first one here is a book
for all of you animal lovers.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:36.035
This is called "Hamsters for
Pleasure and Profit."

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.136
-Come on.

00:00:37.136 --> 00:00:38.638
-I bet this has your usual
advice on how to

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.740
make money off
your hamsters, but who knows.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.443
Let's take a look in here.

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:47.680
Oh. Hmm.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.017
It says, "Begin!

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:55.121
Lose this day loitering,
'twill be the same old story,

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:58.157
tomorrow, and the next day
more dilatory.

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.627
Each indecision brings
its own delays,

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:03.963
and days are lost
lamenting o'er lost days.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:07.299
What you can do,
or think you can, begin it.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:11.370
Boldness has genius,
power, and magic in it!"

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.573
That is a quote by the

00:01:14.573 --> 00:01:18.511
famous 17th century German
writer Goethe.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:23.716
Again, this is "Hamsters for
Pleasure and Profit."

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:28.087
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:31.557
Next up is a photography book.
I love those ones.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:36.596
This one is
called "Women in Trees."

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.664
It is literally 100-plus pages

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:43.669
of old photos of random women
sitting in trees.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:47.874
And in case that
wasn't enough for you,

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.275
they came out with

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:53.246
"More Women in Trees."

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.550
Yeah.

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:04.490
That's actually more of a stump.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.493
-Yeah, sequels are
never as good.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.596
Next is a paranormal book.
It's perfect for Halloween.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.965
This is...

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:17.169
"Enjoy Your Own Funeral."

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.671
Sounds like a fun thing to do.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:23.276
Look at these two people.
They're clearly having a blast.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.079
You should be able to
enjoy your funeral.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.715
It's your day, you know?
-Yeah.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.884
-Why should everyone else
have all the fun?

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:33.920
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.128
Why let everyone else
have the fun?

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:45.764
Next is a book called...

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.535
"Is Eating People Wrong?"

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.171
I'm gonna save you
the time reading this.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.174
Uh, yes.

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.145
I'm not sure what category
this next book belongs in,

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.180
but this is...

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.383
"This Man Touched Me."

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.984
-Come on.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:09.989
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.525
-Yeah. But you know what's
even crazier, though?

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.625
Shocking about this.

00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:16.029
No one checked it out.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.735
Well, we're down to
our last book.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.670
-Oh, man.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.172
-Well, it has --
You know, all good things.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.941
-Yeah.
-This is an autobiography.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:29.942
Yep.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.944
This is called...

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.613
"A Tramp Finds a Home."

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.715
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:47.694
Let's just hope she doesn't
live next to this guy.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.063
There you go.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:53.065
That's all I have for
this edition of my

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.266
"Do Not Read" list.

00:03:54.266 --> 00:03:55.634
If you have a book that
you think should be

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.870
on our next "Do Not Read" list,
I want to see it.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.873 line:0%
Send your titles to
donotread@tonightshow.com.

